%% Figure 2: Global UML Use Case Diagram (Global Use Case Diagram)
%% JC2001 Group 5 / StudyGraph Smart Study Assistant
%% Notes:
%%   1. The <<include>> / <<extend>> stereotypes render with ASCII angle brackets. Mermaid's HTML tag
%%      sanitizer strips <...> inside edge labels as unknown tags, so the source uses monospace placeholders
%%      [[ST_INCLUDE]] / [[ST_EXTEND]], which tools/render_figures.mjs substitutes at export time
%%      with the real stereotypes and fixes the label widths accordingly; when previewing directly in mermaid.live, substitute them by hand.
%%   2. Relationship direction follows the UML 2.5 specification: an include relationship (<<include>>) points from the base use case to the included use case;
%%      an extend relationship (<<extend>>) points from the extending use case to the base use case.
%%   3. The dashed box is the system boundary; status markers are listed below.
%%      [Implemented] delivered in the current PoC; [Frontend-computed] no backend endpoint; [Planned] a later iteration.
flowchart LR
    Student(["University Student<br/>(Student)"])

    subgraph Core["StudyGraph Core Functional Domain (System Boundary)"]
        direction LR
        UC02["<b>UC-02 Targeted Self-Test Practice</b><br/>[Implemented]"]
        UC05["<b>UC-05 View Learning Mastery Radar</b><br/>[Frontend-computed · no backend endpoint]"]
        UC03["<b>UC-03 Search Exam Topics and Concepts</b><br/>[Implemented]"]
        UC01["<b>UC-01 Intelligent Wrong-Answer Trap Diagnosis</b><br/>[Implemented]"]
        UC04["<b>UC-04 Browse Graph Topology Relations</b><br/>[Implemented]"]
        UC08["<b>UC-08 Socratic Tutor Follow-Up</b><br/>[Implemented · local-first]"]
        UC07["<b>UC-07 Adaptive Variant-Question Reinforcement</b><br/>[Planned]"]
        UC06["<b>UC-06 External Model Enhancement</b><br/>[Optional · planned]"]
    end

    Student --> UC02
    Student --> UC05
    Student --> UC03

    UC02 -. "[[ST_INCLUDE]]" .-> UC01
    UC03 -. "[[ST_INCLUDE]]" .-> UC04
    UC08 -. "[[ST_EXTEND]]" .-> UC01
    UC07 -. "[[ST_EXTEND]]" .-> UC01
    UC06 -. "[[ST_EXTEND]]" .-> UC01
    UC06 -. "[[ST_EXTEND]]" .-> UC08

